Requirements: 25   with obligations: 24   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] A requirement that yields one obligation is not read as yielding two.
    -> preserve-decomposition-accuracy-measurement  [compatibility/explicit]   (also serves exclusion-06)
       The change does not alter measuring how accurate decomposition is.

[constraint-01] A requirement's obligations are read as a first obligation followed by
    the remaining ones, so a first obligation that reappears at the head of the
    remainder is one obligation, not two.
    -> first-and-remainder-deduplication  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement's obligations are interpreted as a first obligation followed by the
       remaining ones, and an exact reappearance of that first obligation at the head of
       the remainder is treated as one obligation.
    -> head-repeat-counts-as-one  [functional/explicit]
       A first obligation that reappears at the head of the remainder is treated as one
       obligation rather than two.
    -> repeat-head-counts-as-one  [invariant/inferred]
       A first obligation that reappears at the head of the remainder is treated as the
       same obligation, not a second one.

[constraint-02] A remaining obligation is a repeat of the first only when every one of
    its fields is exactly equal to the first's.
    -> exact-field-equality-repeat  [invariant/explicit]
       A remaining obligation is treated as a repeat of the first only when every field
       is exactly equal to the first's fields.
    -> exact-field-equality-for-repeat  [invariant/explicit]
       A remaining obligation is considered a repeat of the first only when every field
       is exactly equal to the first obligation's fields.

[constraint-03] A remaining obligation that differs from the first in any field is kept,
    however similarly it reads.
    -> field-difference-keeps-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       A remaining obligation that differs from the first in any field is kept as a
       distinct obligation, regardless of similarity in wording.

[constraint-04] Only a repeat at the head of the remainder is read as a repeat; the same
    obligation appearing anywhere later is kept.
    -> only-head-repeat-is-merged  [functional/explicit]
       Only a repeat at the head of the remainder is treated as a repeat; the same
       obligation appearing later in the remainder is kept.

[constraint-05] Reading a repeated obligation as one is recorded, and the record
    attributes it to the shape of the response rather than to a faulty answer.
    -> repeat-dedup-recorded-as-shape  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Reading a repeated obligation as one is recorded, and the record attributes that
       outcome to the shape of the response rather than to a faulty answer.

[constraint-06] A requirement that yielded obligations is never left holding none.
    -> yielded-requirement-never-empty  [invariant/explicit]
       A requirement that yields obligations always retains at least one obligation.

[constraint-07] The obligation that survives keeps its own content unchanged.
    -> surviving-obligation-content-preserved  [invariant/explicit]
       The obligation that survives keeps its own content unchanged.

[constraint-08] The obligation that survives carries no disambiguating identifier suffix
    that was earned only by a repeat.
    -> no-repeat-earned-suffix-on-survivor  [invariant/explicit]
       The surviving obligation carries no disambiguating identifier suffix that was
       earned only by a repeat.

[constraint-09] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-review-state  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state.

[constraint-10] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> no-live-model-calls-in-tests  [functional/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

